# Bright Nexa School OS — example deployment settings
# Copy this file to .env for LOCAL DEVELOPMENT only. Never commit .env or live secrets.
#
# Node / SQLite pilot backend:
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000

# Generate each secret independently (minimum 32 cryptographically random bytes).
# Node example: node -e "console.log(require('node:crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# SESSION_SECRET=<generated random secret>
# ADMIN_API_KEY=<generated independent random secret>
#
# IMPORTANT: the pilot server currently loads process.env, not a dotenv file.
# Set these in the shell/process manager or Render environment settings instead
# of assuming that merely copying this example activates the variables.
#
# Supabase/cloud teacher portal:
# Supabase URL and PUBLISHABLE API key are public frontend configuration,
# not credentials. Never put SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, sb_secret_*,
# database passwords or private signing keys into public JS or HTML.
# Supabase Edge Functions receive managed SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
# / SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY as server-side function environment settings.
#
# Production cloud school management requires:
# - verified Supabase Auth accounts and tenant-bound membership
# - Row Level Security on all institution tables
# - HTTPS-only transport and approved Auth redirect URLs
# - durable databases and key rotation / backup procedures
